Michelle:

Continuing with the minke data example from the vignette, to get all the details of the chi-square GOF, you want this:

> whales <- read.csv("minke.csv")
> whale.trunc <- 1.5
> whale.pooledf0 <- ds(whales, truncation=whale.trunc, key="hr",  adjustment=NULL)
Fitting hazard-rate key function
AIC= 48.638
> fit.pooled <- ddf.gof(whale.pooledf0$ddf)
> fit.pooled$chisquare
$chi1
$chi1$observed

    [0,0.167] (0.167,0.333]   (0.333,0.5]   (0.5,0.667] (0.667,0.833]     (0.833,1]      (1,1.17]
           20            11            16            14             7            10             3
  (1.17,1.33]    (1.33,1.5]
            4             3

$chi1$expected
[1] 15.709224 15.708874 15.441474 13.276153  9.822874  6.922222  4.907293  3.560244  2.651642

$chi1$chisq
[1] 5.664229

$chi1$p
[1] 0.4618338

$chi1$df
[1] 6

